==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*þunkijaną}}. Cognate with Old Saxon [[thunkian]] (Dutch [[dunken]]), Old High German [[thunken]] (German [[dünken]]), Old Norse [[þykkja]] (Swedish [[tycka]], Norwegian Nynorsk {{l|nn|tykkja}}), Gothic [[𐌸𐌿𐌲𐌺𐌾𐌰𐌽]], Limburgish [[tönk]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈθynt͡ʃɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|head=þynċan}}

# {{context|impersonal|lang=ang}} to [[seem]], [[appear]] (''+ dative'')

